EVERY FILE UNDER vendor/ IS A VERBATIM COPY. DO NOT EDIT ANY OF THEM.

The harness never modifies engine files and never reimplements engine logic.
It drives the real page the same way a human does: it fills in the Custom Mod
Loader textareas, clicks "Play Custom Mod", clicks through the selection
screens, and clicks answer buttons. The simulation, the turn loop
(nextQuestion), the CYOA dispatch, and the vote math (A()) are all upstream
code running unmodified.

Layout mirrors upstream exactly so that the relative paths inside
campaign-trail/index.html resolve without rewriting:

  campaign-trail/index.html                  the real game page
  static/js/*.js                             engine
  static/js/lib/raphael.js                   map renderer
  static/js/us-map-1.0.1/jquery.usmap.js     map plugin (loaded by the questionset)
  static/json/*.json                         base election/candidate data
  static/questionset/2020_Biden_Bass.html    base 2020 questionset (see below)
  static/*.css, static/css/*.css             stylesheets
  ajax.googleapis.com/.../jquery.min.js      jQuery 1.11.1

Why the base questionset is vendored
------------------------------------
For a modded 2020 Biden ticket the engine resolves the questionset filename
through baseScenarioDict and lands on 2020_Biden_Bass.html. It loads that file
into #game_window FIRST, then runs your Code 2 over the top. Three consequences,
all of which the harness depends on:

  1. Your Code 2 inherits four values it never sets itself:
       answer_feedback_flg = 1     (without this, no advisor feedback ever shows)
       player_answers      = []
       player_visits       = []
       game_start_logging_id
  2. Any base field your Code 2 does not override stays at the base value.
  3. The questionset is what loads the us-map plugin. Without it the map
     never initialises and the poll screens throw.

Files deliberately NOT vendored
-------------------------------
Two scripts are fetched from a CDN by campaign-trail/index.html and are not in
this folder:
  https://code.jquery.com/jquery-4.0.0.min.js
  https://code.jquery.com/ui/1.14.1/jquery-ui.min.js
Google Fonts (Montserrat) is also remote — your Code 1 imports it too.
So the FIRST load needs an internet connection. After that the browser caches
them and you can work offline. This is the one external dependency; see the
"when things break" section of the README.

Images are not vendored. Missing images 404 harmlessly and show as broken
image icons. Nothing functional depends on them.

Verifying this copy is untouched
--------------------------------
    cd playtest/engine/vendor && shasum -a 256 -c ../MANIFEST.sha256

Re-pinning to a newer upstream
------------------------------
See "What to do if the upstream engine changes" in ../README.md. Short version:
re-clone, re-copy, regenerate MANIFEST.sha256, update this file, then run the
parity check to see whether the numbers moved.
